              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em simplicial groupoids
            pairs the concepts of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+loop+groupoid"} Dwyer-Kan loop groupoid
            functor &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKan84"}> Dwyer &amp; Kan (1984)
            \&amp;rbrack; their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            theory is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical
            homotopy theory of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
            (both being models for
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoids"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-groupoids
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            A priori, the term
            %em simplicial groupoid
            may refer to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            in the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"}> 1-
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"}> small
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
          %p
            However (cf. discussion at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+category"} simplicial category
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %em simplicially constant
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"}> sSet
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+groupoids"} enriched groupoids
            — is traditionally still referred to as “simplicial groupoids” &amp;lbrack;e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DwyerKan84"} Dwyer &amp; Kan (1984), §1.2.(ii)
            = succeed "&rbrack;;" do
              %a{:href => "GoerssJardine09"} Goerss &amp; Jardine (2009), V.7
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            they form by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                  %mtext -
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi sGrpd
                    %mi DK
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sSet\text{-}Grpd
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  sGrpd_{DK}
                  \\overset{\phantom{---}}{\hookrightarrow}
                  Func(\Delta^{op}, Grpd)
                  \\,.
          %p
            So given such a simplicial DK-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi sGrpd
                    %mi DK
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_\bullet \,\in\, sGrpd_{DK}
            we have:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a plain
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Obj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi Sets
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(\mathcal{C}_\bullet) \,\in\, Sets
            %li
              %p
                for every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi Obj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \,\in\, Obj(\mathcal{C}_\bullet)
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                the degree-wise
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
                form a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi sSet
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ;
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathcal{C}_\bullet(x,y)
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      Hom_{\mathcal{C}_\bullet}(x,y)
                      \\;\in\;
                      sSet
                      \\,;
            %li
              %p
                where the degreewise
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                operations constitutes an
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
                composition operation
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ×
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathcal{C}_\bullet(x,y)
                      \\,\times\,
                      \\mathcal{C}_\bullet(y,z)
                      \\overset{\circ}{\longrightarrow}
                      \\mathcal{C}_\bullet(x,z)
            %li
              %p
                making
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_\bullet
                an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+category"} sSet-enriched category
          %p
            Conversely, simplical DK-groupoids are therefore in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            to those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+categories"} sSet-enriched categories
            whose degreewise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            formed by the
            = succeed "-cell" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \,\in\, \mathbb{N}
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
          %p
            This makes the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sGrpd
                    %mi DK
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sGrpd_{DK}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the category of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"}> small
            )
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+categories"} sSet-enriched categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sGrpd
                    %mi DK
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi sSet
                  %mi Cat
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sGrpd_{DK}
                  \\overset{\phantom{---}}{\hookrightarrow}
                  sSet Cat
                  \\,.
          %h2#remarks Remarks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Simplicially enriched groupoids are related to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial sets
                via an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
                found independently by Dwyer &amp; Kan and Joyal &amp; Tierney; see
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+loop+groupoid"} Dwyer-Kan loop groupoid
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy categories
                so that simplicially enriched groupoids model all
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy types
              %ul
                %li
                  This is a groupoidal version of the equivalence between
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-categories
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched categories
                  via the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
            %li
              %p
                A simplicially enriched groupoid having exactly one object is essentially the same as a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            %li
              %p
                Many constructions on simplicial groups, such as that of its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
                carry over to simplicialy enriched groupoids without difficulty.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToSimplicialGroups Relation to simplicial groups
          %p
          #SimplicialDeloopingGroupoids.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoid"} simplicial
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoid"} delooping groupoid
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} \,\in\, Grp(sSet)
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoid"} delooping groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathcal{G}
              by setting
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Obj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(\mathbf{B}\mathcal{G}) \,\coloneqq\, \ast
                  (the
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+set"} singleton set
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mo ,
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}\mathcal{G})(\ast,\ast) \,\coloneqq\, \mathcal{G}
              %li
                %p
                  with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  given by the group operation of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒢
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            %p
              Conversely, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi sSet
